#compdef await

# Block on a job started by `async`, print its captured stdout and return
# its exit status: `await $id`.
#
# zshrs builtin. builtin_await (src/extensions/ext_builtins.rs) takes no
# options and reads only the first argument, a numeric job ID. The IDs live
# in the executor's async_jobs table (src/vm_helper.rs), which no parameter
# or builtin exposes, so they cannot be listed here.
# Bundled into ~/.zshrs/functions by build.rs.

_arguments '1:async job ID (printed by async):'
